    "updated_at": "2016-08-23T08:38:09Z",
    "body": "I don't believe that addresses the problem. `Reflect.construct` allows me to call the function as a constructor, but in the case of calling `customElements.define()`, I'm not the one calling the constructor (or rejecting it for not calling `super()`)--the browser is doing that when it upgrades the element. If I'm wrong, can you provide some sample code to explain?\n",
